# steps SKIP may name, how serious leaving each out is (note / warn), and what changes.
# Every other step is needed by a later one and cannot be skipped.
het	note	no per-individual heterozygosity
theta	note	no pi, Watterson's theta or Tajima's D
groups	note	no FST among sampling groups
fstall	note	no full-panel FST (outliers in) to compare with the neutral FST
symbionts	note	no reads-per-symbiont-genus table
neutral	warn	lineage calls are not re-checked without outliers and kin
kin	warn	related individuals stay in: SFS, theta, Tajima's D and FST will include close kin, which skews allele frequencies toward their families
outliers	warn	SNPs under selection stay in the SFS and FST: demography assumes neutral sites, and lineage FST can be inflated; fstall is skipped as well (it compares outliers in vs out)
fst	warn	no lineage FST, fstall is skipped as well, and the demography pipeline cannot run (it fits the 2D spectra fst makes)
